{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals","id":1435904,"title":"Creating experienced characters / Awakening experienced mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-18T15:31:01-08:00","id":1435904,"title":"Creating experienced characters / Awakening experienced mortals","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> What are the rules for those that awakened later in life? In this case existing experienced mortals.<br /> <br /> Do they get the mage template (extra resistance attribute dot, Gnosis 1, 6 Arcana dots, and 3 extra merit dots) and after being inducted to an Order: Rotes + High Speech + Initial status dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T15:38:15-08:00","id":1435908,"title":"","content":"They don't get the difference in starting Merit dots, but otherwise yes, you just give a mortal that Awakens the starting Mage template (presuming they have some source of training), though lots of groups will introduce things slowly over a few sessions rather than dump on everything at once.<br /> <br /> More experienced characters in general are handled by just giving out starting XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T16:44:31-08:00","id":1435912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals#post1435904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> What are the rules for those that awakened later in life? In this case existing experienced mortals.<br /> <br /> Do they get the mage template (extra resistance attribute dot, Gnosis 1, 6 Arcana dots, and 3 extra merit dots) and after being inducted to an Order: Rotes + High Speech + Initial status dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to signs and sorcery it's gnosis 1, 3 arcana (1 in one ruling, 2 in the other), and 1 resolve or composure. There are also additional addons to awakenings that can grant familiars/artifacts/ move around dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T16:48:52-08:00","id":1435913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals#post1435904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> What are the rules for those that awakened later in life? In this case existing experienced mortals.<br /> <br /> Do they get the mage template (extra resistance attribute dot, Gnosis 1, 6 Arcana dots, and 3 extra merit dots) and after being inducted to an Order: Rotes + High Speech + Initial status dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s rules for newly Awakened characters in Signs of Sorcery pg. 133. In short, a new mage only gets three Arcana dots, 1 Gnosis, 8 Wisdom, the extra Resistance dot, and nothing else. The core template, on the other hand, assumes the character has had some training and a few months experience. Depending on the circumstances of your game, either template may be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T18:02:15-08:00","id":1435924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals?p=1435908#post1435908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't get the difference in starting Merit dots</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because mortals start with 7 Merit dots at character creation, while supernaturals tend to have 10.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T09:20:47-08:00","id":1436026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals?p=1435924#post1435924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because mortals start with 7 Merit dots at character creation, while supernaturals tend to have 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, mortal creation has 7 merit dots, and all supernaturals get 10. So I expected mortals to get the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T10:56:47-08:00","id":1436042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals?p=1436026#post1436026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, mortal creation has 7 merit dots, and all supernaturals get 10. So I expected mortals to get the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those extra dots are for the player's benefit. Supernaturals have access not only to almost all mundane Merits that are available for mortals but also a whole slew of new Merits specific to their template. Increasing the free dots allows players to add things like Shadow Name, Occultation, a location Merit (Hallow/Sanctum/Demesne), an item Merit (Artifact/Enhanced Item/Grimoire/Imbued Item) and/or an Order Merit (Adamant Hand/Egregore/Lex Magica/Masque/Prelacy/Techn\u00e9) while still having a little room for mundane Merits. Mage especially is ridiculous in the amount of Merits you'd potentially want for your character.<br /> Supernatural Merits are exclusive for mortals (generally) but in my experience they're far less common (and often disallowed in many games that focuses on street level play) and when they are used it's rarely more than a single Merit. That's in stark contrast to how you could easily spend more than your three extra dots on Mage exclusive Merits when creating a character.<br /> <br /> But in-setting there's no reason for a newly Awakened mage to gain any extra Merit dots at all.<br /> <br /> If you want to be generous anyway you could grant a rebate of sorts. For the first six dots of Mage exclusive Merits they buy they don't have to spend XP to gain the second, fourth or sixth dots. Otherwise, as already mentioned above, more experienced characters just start with more XP. The standard bonus XP is 5/10/15/25/35/50/100 depending on how experienced. That table isn't reproduced in Mage, probably because of word count and having to juggle two different XP types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T16:45:10-08:00","id":1436321,"title":"","content":"Yeah - the main rulebook's template assumes a year or so of training by an Order until the new mage is ready to go out on their own, while the one in Signs of Sorcery is for the very instant after their Awakening. If you're running a Chronicle where an existing character will Awaken, use the Signs of Sorcery one unless you want to time-skip their basic training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T18:22:21-08:00","id":1436343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals?p=1436321#post1436321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - the main rulebook's template assumes a year or so of training by an Order until the new mage is ready to go out on their own, while the one in Signs of Sorcery is for the very instant after their Awakening. If you're running a Chronicle where an existing character will Awaken, use the Signs of Sorcery one unless you want to time-skip their basic training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer!<br /> <br /> Would you make the additional 3 dots of merits that Supernaturals get over mortals, as part of that year for an experience mortal character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T11:34:34-08:00","id":1436565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1435904-creating-experienced-characters-awakening-experienced-mortals?p=1436343#post1436343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer!<br /> <br /> Would you make the additional 3 dots of merits that Supernaturals get over mortals, as part of that year for an experience mortal character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would lean towards giving them a free dot of order status if they join an order, and maybe artifact dots if they undergo a metamorphic awakening. I'd let them take merit dots for magical merits in general, but everything besides maybe Status and Shadow name is throw into xp debt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}